description:
Change under review: let partner dashboards call the account API from the browser. Added files are shown in full. For changed files, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file is unchanged and compiles.

`src/http/cors.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import type { Handler } from "./types.js";
2
3 const PARTNER_ORIGIN = /^https:\/\/[a-z0-9-]+.example.com$/;
4
5 export function withCors(handler: Handler): Handler {
6   return async (req) => {
7     const origin = req.headers.get("origin") ?? "";
8     const res = req.method === "OPTIONS" ? new Response(null, { status: 204 }) : await handler(req);
9     if (PARTNER_ORIGIN.test(origin)) {
10       res.headers.set("Access-Control-Allow-Origin", origin);
11       res.headers.set("Access-Control-Allow-Credentials", "true");
12       res.headers.set("Access-Control-Allow-Headers", "content-type");
13       res.headers.set("Access-Control-Allow-Methods", "GET, POST");
14       res.headers.set("Vary", "Origin");
15     }
16     return res;
17   };
18 }
```

`src/server.ts` (changed, line 22):
```ts
22 router.all("/api/account/*", withCors(accountRoutes));
```

Each partner's dashboard is served from its own subdomain, such as `https://acme.example.com`; only the company creates subdomains of `example.com`. The account API authenticates with the `session` cookie (`Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=None`). It serves `GET /api/account/profile` (name, email address and the names of the user's API keys) and `POST /api/account/email` (changes the login email address).
